# Computer Vision App with Azure Cognitive Services

A guided project completed as part of a Microsoft-authored course on Coursera, focused on building a computer vision application using **Azure Cognitive Services**.

## 📌 Overview
This project explored how to integrate Microsoft Azure's pre-built AI models into an application to perform image analysis tasks — such as object detection, image tagging, and extracting descriptive metadata from images — without training a model from scratch.

## 🧠 What I Learned
- Setting up and configuring an Azure Cognitive Services resource
- Making API calls to Azure's Computer Vision endpoint
- Parsing and using the JSON responses (tags, descriptions, detected objects)
- Understanding how cloud-hosted AI services can be integrated into real applications
- Practical exposure to Microsoft's Azure ecosystem, relevant to both AI and cloud security work

## 🛠️ Tech / Tools
- Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services (Computer Vision API)
- Coursera guided project environment

## 📜 Certificate
Completed **Sep 2026** — [Verify on Coursera](https://coursera.org/verify/OQ8EHMSU81FB)

